// activediq.connector.v1 — Plan and Apply (the write group, contract v1.1, T-0091; v1.2, T-0122).
//
// The operation pipeline (ADR-0005) calls Plan while it plans a step: the connector re-reads the
// target live on the pinned DC, evaluates tier0 on its own (TM-D2 check 1 runs on this live read)
// and returns the before-state precondition. The pipeline then calls Apply, through
// `directory/client.Write` with a Clearance only (ADR-0005 rule 2, O2), with that precondition;
// the connector repeats every check and performs the conditional write of ADR-0005 rule 4 only if
// the target is unchanged and not tier0. The connector keeps no plan state: Apply stands on its own.
//
// Invariants (connector-contract.md §8):
//   * A tier0 target fails with ERROR_CODE_TIER0_REFUSED and no directory write, whatever the
//     server asks (TM-D2). Every object the typed change touches is evaluated, not only `target`.
//   * Plan and Apply fail with ERROR_CODE_ACTIVATION_REFUSED_OVERPRIVILEGED while the connector's
//     own last VerifyConnection for the connection does not open its write gate (DM-10.I11).
//   * No credential material travels in these messages (fitness-proto P7). A write kind that sets a
//     secret (password reset) needs its own sealed-secret shape and a security-architect review.
//   * The touched set is derived by the connector from the typed change, never from a list the
//     server sends. Tier0Context carries one CorrelationStatement per touched object; a touched
